<!--
    TreeSwitch: a binary-search compare tree of two cases.

    Authored x86-64 (GNU as): `cmp $0,%edi; jg` splits the range, each side tests
    one equality (0 or 1) and falls to one shared default block that returns 9.
    gcc -O0 lowers a dense switch this way, with no jump table.

    Default: the tree stays an if/else chain (the cascade has 2 cases, below the
    shipped floor of 3). `option treeswitch 2` lowers the floor to 2, so the same
    tree re-rolls into a switch.
-->
